m{ZF}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\)</span> (the metatheoretically generated first-order theory defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zermelo\\text{-}fraenkel}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\mathrm{ZF}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\coloneqq{}&amp;\\mathrm{FOL}_{=} (\\Sigma_{\\in})+\\{\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}ext},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}pair},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}union},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}pow},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}inf},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}reg}\\}\\\\\n&amp;+\\{\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}sep}[\\varphi]:\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})\\}\n+\\{\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}rep}[\\varphi]:\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zermelo\\text{-}fraenkel}\\vdash_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\mathrm{ZF}_{\\mathrm{meta}}\\coloneqq{}&amp;\\mathrm{FOL}_{=} (\\Sigma_{\\in})+\\{\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}ext},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}pair},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}union},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}pow},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}inf},\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}reg}\\}\\\\\n&amp;+\\{\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}sep}[\\varphi]:\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})\\}\n+\\{\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}rep}[\\varphi]:\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>ZF is a metalinguistically generated theory, not an object-language set obtained by unioning undeclared symbols <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AxSep}\">\\(\\mathrm{AxSep}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AxRep}\">\\(\\mathrm{AxRep}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>ZFC is obtained from ZF by adding the axiom of choice.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":